    <item>
      <title>Purview retires four DSPM partner integrations December 7 as permissions auditing expands — 9 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 9 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Purview retires four DSPM partner integrations December 7 as permissions auditing expands</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">Microsoft Purview will retire its Varonis, BigID, Cyera, and OneTrust DSPM integrations for non-Microsoft data sources on December 7, 2026. Separately, Purview is adding two audit operations for role-based access control, with worldwide rollout scheduled from late September through mid-November 2026.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/purview.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Purview · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/#MC1545691" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Four DSPM partner integrations will retire</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">On December 7, 2026, Purview will retire the Varonis, BigID, Cyera, and OneTrust integrations for non-Microsoft data sources. They will no longer ingest or display data; other DSPM capabilities remain unaffected. Microsoft says no action is required, but administrators should review dependencies if they use these integrations.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/purview.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Purview · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/#MC1473155" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">RBAC permissions auditing gains two operations</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Purview is adding two new audit operations for role-based access control, improving transparency and troubleshooting for access issues. The enhancement is rolling out worldwide from late September through mid-November 2026 and requires no administrator action.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 9 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 9 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Purview retires four DSPM partner integrations December 7 as permissions auditing expands</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">Microsoft Purview will retire its Varonis, BigID, Cyera, and OneTrust DSPM integrations for non-Microsoft data sources on December 7, 2026. Separately, Purview is adding two audit operations for role-based access control, with worldwide rollout scheduled from late September through mid-November 2026.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/purview.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Purview · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/#MC1545691" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Four DSPM partner integrations will retire</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">On December 7, 2026, Purview will retire the Varonis, BigID, Cyera, and OneTrust integrations for non-Microsoft data sources. They will no longer ingest or display data; other DSPM capabilities remain unaffected. Microsoft says no action is required, but administrators should review dependencies if they use these integrations.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/purview.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Purview · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/#MC1473155" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">RBAC permissions auditing gains two operations</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Purview is adding two new audit operations for role-based access control, improving transparency and troubleshooting for access issues. The enhancement is rolling out worldwide from late September through mid-November 2026 and requires no administrator action.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 9 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
