    <item>
      <title>DLP adds a control to exclude external emails from Copilot grounding — 6 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 6 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">DLP adds a control to exclude external emails from Copilot grounding</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">A new admin-configurable Purview DLP control is described for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat. It restricts processing of email from external or untrusted domains while preserving internal data use. The period also adds more precise auto-label simulation troubleshooting and a new audit activity for gateway datasource status tests.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/purview.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/ai.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Purview · AI and Copilot</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#MC1301714" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">DLP can exclude external email from Copilot grounding</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Message Center item describes a new admin-configurable DLP control for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat. It excludes email from external or untrusted domains from Copilot grounding while maintaining internal data use; the item lists public preview in June 2026 and general availability in June 2027.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/information-protection.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/classification.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Information Protection · Labels and classification</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-auto-label-simulation-results-03" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Auto-label guidance adds failure and partial-result handling</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Auto Label Simulation Results article adds the “Simulation failed” status, distinguishes failed jobs from requests that could not start, explains partial workload counts, and provides guidance for reviewing or restarting simulations. Administrators are told to preserve useful results before restarting and review workload details before enabling a policy.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/audit.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Audit · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-audit-log-activities-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Audit references gateway datasource status test activity</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Audit Log Activities reference now includes GetGatewayClusterDatasourceStatusAsAdmin for tenant administrator connection status tests, giving administrators the activity name needed to identify those tests in audit records.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/information-protection.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/classification.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Information Protection · Labels and classification</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-apply-sensitivity-label-automatically-02" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Sensitivity-label guidance links simulation failure details</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Apply Sensitivity Label Automatically now links to guidance for simulation failure messages and results marked “(partial)”. The change helps administrators find the relevant troubleshooting guidance when simulations fail or produce partial results.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 6 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 6 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">DLP adds a control to exclude external emails from Copilot grounding</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">A new admin-configurable Purview DLP control is described for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat. It restricts processing of email from external or untrusted domains while preserving internal data use. The period also adds more precise auto-label simulation troubleshooting and a new audit activity for gateway datasource status tests.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/purview.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/ai.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Purview · AI and Copilot</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#MC1301714" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">DLP can exclude external email from Copilot grounding</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Message Center item describes a new admin-configurable DLP control for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat. It excludes email from external or untrusted domains from Copilot grounding while maintaining internal data use; the item lists public preview in June 2026 and general availability in June 2027.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/information-protection.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/classification.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Information Protection · Labels and classification</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-auto-label-simulation-results-03" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Auto-label guidance adds failure and partial-result handling</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Auto Label Simulation Results article adds the “Simulation failed” status, distinguishes failed jobs from requests that could not start, explains partial workload counts, and provides guidance for reviewing or restarting simulations. Administrators are told to preserve useful results before restarting and review workload details before enabling a policy.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/audit.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Audit · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-audit-log-activities-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Audit references gateway datasource status test activity</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Audit Log Activities reference now includes GetGatewayClusterDatasourceStatusAsAdmin for tenant administrator connection status tests, giving administrators the activity name needed to identify those tests in audit records.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/information-protection.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/classification.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Information Protection · Labels and classification</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-apply-sensitivity-label-automatically-02" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Sensitivity-label guidance links simulation failure details</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Apply Sensitivity Label Automatically now links to guidance for simulation failure messages and results marked “(partial)”. The change helps administrators find the relevant troubleshooting guidance when simulations fail or produce partial results.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 6 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
