    <item>
      <title>Purview retention splits Copilot coverage; auto-labeling capped at 500,000 files daily — 5 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 5 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Purview retention splits Copilot coverage; auto-labeling capped at 500,000 files daily</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">Two administrator-relevant updates stand out. Beginning January 15, 2027, the “Teams chats and Copilot interactions” retention location will cover Teams content only, while updated Information Protection guidance defines 500,000 automatically labeled SharePoint and OneDrive files per tenant per day as an absolute aggregate ceiling across all auto-labeling policies, not a guaranteed processing rate. Related Purview pages now reflect the same ceiling.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/data-lifecycle-management.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/policies.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Data Lifecycle · Policies and rules</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/#doc-2026-11-05-create-retention-policies-04" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Teams and Copilot retention coverage separates on January 15, 2027</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Policies using “Teams chats and Copilot interactions” will apply only to Teams content beginning January 15, 2027. They will no longer retain or delete Microsoft 365 Copilot interactions, including previously retained interactions. Use the separate “Microsoft Copilot Experiences” location when Copilot retention is required.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/products/information-protection.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.purview.admin.news/assets/topics/classification.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Information Protection · Labels and classification</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/#doc-2026-11-05-apply-sensitivity-label-automatically-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Auto-labeling throughput is an aggregate tenant ceiling, not a rate</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The limit for automatically labeled SharePoint and OneDrive files is stated as an absolute maximum of 500,000 files per tenant per day across all auto-labeling policies. Actual throughput may be lower, so administrators should assess volume across the tenant rather than treating the figure as an expected daily processing rate.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 5 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
