/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Information Protection · Labels and classification</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/#doc-2026-11-05-apply-sensitivity-label-automatically-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Auto-labeling throughput is an aggregate tenant ceiling, not a rate</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The limit for automatically labeled SharePoint and OneDrive files is stated as an absolute maximum of 500,000 files per tenant per day across all auto-labeling policies. Actual throughput may be lower, so administrators should assess volume across the tenant rather than treating the figure as an expected daily processing rate.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.purview.admin.news/day/2026-11-05/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 5 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
